msgid "<0>Temperature:</0> Celsius, Fahrenheit, Kelvin, and Newton."
msgstr "<0>Température :</0> Celsius, Fahrenheit, Kelvin et Newton."

#: src/components/website-description.tsx:68
msgid "<0>Ultimate Precision:</0> Powered by Decimal.js for zero rounding errors."
msgstr "<0>Ultimate Precision :</0> Alimenté par Decimal.js pour zéro erreur d'arrondi."

#: src/routes/$lang/privacy-policy.tsx:97
msgid "<0>Usage data:</0> pages viewed, approximate location derived from IP, device/browser type, and referral information — typically via analytics tools after you consent."
msgstr "<0>Données d'utilisation :</0> pages consultées, emplacement approximatif dérivé de l'adresse IP, du type d'appareil/navigateur et informations de référence - généralement via des outils d'analyse après votre consentement."

#: src/components/website-description.tsx:53
msgid "<0>Volume:</0> Litres, Cubic Inches, Gallons, and Millilitres."
msgstr "<0>Volume :</0> Litres, pouces cubes, gallons et millilitres."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:371
msgid "0.25 g of caffeine powder is 250 mg—matching many anhydrous caffeine capsule labels. A 1.5 g electrolyte packet is 1,500 mg of total salts before splitting components."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:809
msgid "1 ha = 10 000 m². 1 km² = 100 ha = 1 000 000 m². 1 acre ≈ 0.404 686 ha. 1 acre ≈ 4 047 m² (more precisely 4 046.856 422 4 m²). 1 acre = 43 560 ft² by definition in US customary land measure tied to the survey/international foot discussion. Memorise the hectare and the acre-to-square-metre pair; derive the rest when needed."
msgstr "1 ha = 10 000 m². 1 km² = 100 ha = 1 000 000 m². 1 acre ≈ 0,404 686 ha. 1 acre ≈ 4 047 m² (plus précisément 4 046.856 422 4 m²). 1 acre = 43 560 pi² par définition dans la mesure foncière coutumière américaine liée à l'enquête/à la discussion internationale. Mémorisez l’hectare et le couple acre/mètre carré ; dériver le reste en cas de besoin."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1942
msgid "1 Julian year = 365.25 days = 8,766 hours = 525,960 minutes = 31,557,600 seconds. Those relationships are exact under the definition used here. Converters that implement Year (Julian) should match these figures."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:489
msgid "1 Julian year is 365.25 days. 4 Julian years are 1,461 days—the leap-day pattern baked into that average."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2017
msgid "1 m² ≈ 10.7639 ft². 1 ft² ≈ 0.092903 m². Those factors are squares of the metre–foot length relationship. That is why a “10% longer room” is not a “10% larger carpet order” when you also change width."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2392
msgid "1 m³ = 1,000 L = 1,000,000 mL. Those metric relationships are exact. Convert volume into the unit that matches your density’s denominator before multiplying."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:359
msgid "1.2 kg of sugar for syrup is 1,200 g on a recipe card. A 0.025 kg spice purchase is 25 g—typical jar size."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:427
msgid "10 m/s is about 22.4 mph—a stiff cycling headwind. Terminal-velocity ballpark 50 m/s is roughly 112 mph before posture and drag details."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2183
msgid "10 st ≈ 63.5 kg ≈ 140 lb; 11 st ≈ 69.9 kg ≈ 154 lb; 12 st ≈ 76.2 kg ≈ 168 lb; 14 st ≈ 88.9 kg ≈ 196 lb. Anchors help conversation; exact converters help forms."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:335
msgid "10 stone is 63.5 kg. Someone at 13 st 7 lb is 13.5 stone ≈ 85.7 kg for a metric hospital chart."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:261
msgid "120 mL of oil is ½ US cup (240 mL cup). A 15 mL vanilla note is 1 tablespoon, not a full cup—sanity-check small millilitre amounts before calling them cups."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:447
msgid "150 seconds of rest is 2.5 minutes between sets. A 3,600-second timeout is 60 minutes—one hour for a long job."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:501
msgid "2 hours of battery life claimed is 7,200 seconds of runtime budget. A 0.25-hour quiz is 900 seconds on an auto-submit timer."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:279
msgid "2 metric tablespoons of olive oil equal 6 metric teaspoons—handy when you only have a 5 mL spoon. A recipe calling for 1½ tbsp yeast is 4.5 tsp."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:483
msgid "21 days of meal prep is 3 weeks. A 10-day antibiotic leftover discussion is about 1.43 weeks—usually left in days for clarity."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:433
msgid "30 mph is about 13.4 m/s for a urban crash energy sketch. A 100 mph pitch (extreme) would be ~44.7 m/s—far above normal baseball, showing why unit checks matter."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1403
msgid "350 °F converts to about 177 °C, commonly rounded to 180 °C in home recipes. Confirm with your oven and recipe style."
msgstr "350 °F se convertit en environ 177 °C, généralement arrondi à 180 °C dans les recettes maison. Confirmez avec votre four et votre style de recette."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:421
msgid "37 km/h wind is 20 knots—common small-craft advisory territory depending on local rules. A ferry at 40 km/h is about 21.6 kn."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:409
msgid "44 ft/s is 30 mph—a common residential speed comparison. A fall speed of 100 ft/s is about 68 mph before drag limits."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:471
msgid "48 hours of ferment time is 2 days on a kitchen calendar. A 168-hour work stretch is 7 days—one full week of continuous hours."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1285
msgid "5 ft 10 in is 70 inches total. One international inch is 2.54 cm, so 70 × 2.54 = 177.8 cm. Round according to the form’s rules."
msgstr "5 pieds 10 pouces correspondent à 70 pouces au total. Un pouce international mesure 2,54 cm, donc 70 × 2,54 = 177,8 cm. Arrondissez selon les règles de la forme."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:403
msgid "60 mph is exactly 88 ft/s—the classic driving-physics mnemonic. A baseball at 90 mph is 132 ft/s toward the plate."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:507
msgid "7,200 seconds of encode time is 2 hours. A 540-second kilometer split talk converts to 0.15 hours only if you truly need hours—minutes are usually clearer."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:329
msgid "70 kg is about 11 stone 0 lb (11.02 st). A fighter listed at 12 stone is 76.2 kg—useful when comparing to metric weight classes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:385
msgid "70 mph on an interstate is about 113 km/h. A 6 mph walking pace is roughly 9.7 km/h for metric fitness watches."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:495
msgid "730.5 days is 2 Julian years. A 10,000-day time series spans about 27.38 Julian years—handy for long climate annotations."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:285
msgid "9 metric teaspoons of cocoa is 3 metric tablespoons for a brownie batch. A ½ tsp salt pinch is 1/6 tablespoon—usually left as teaspoons for readability."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:397
msgid "90 km/h traffic is 25 m/s—handy for estimating stopping-distance thought experiments. A 18 km/h bike speed is 5 m/s."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:459
msgid "90 minutes of parking is 1.5 hours on a meter that bills hourly. A 105-minute feature film is 1.75 hours."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2453
msgid "A “5:00 min/km” pace is 12 km/h. A “8:00 min/mile” pace is 7.5 mph. Those are different efforts—convert carefully before you race your training partners’ screenshots."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:193
msgid "A 1,000 km² national park is about 386 sq mi. A wildfire mapped at 50 km² covers roughly 19.3 sq mi for US incident reports."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:175
msgid "A 1,200 sq ft bungalow is about 111.5 m² for a European energy certificate. A 200 sq ft deck needs about 18.6 m² of board coverage before waste."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:249
msgid "A 1.5 L soft drink is 1,500 mL for calorie apps that expect millilitres. Mixing 0.25 L of stock means 250 mL on a kitchen measuring jug."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:45
msgid "A ¼-20 tap drill often uses a 0.201″ hole, about 5.11 mm—handy when your metric drill set jumps in 0.1 mm steps. Plywood sold as ¾ inch is 19.05 mm; European 18 mm sheet is close but not identical for tight dados."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:187
msgid "A 10 ha orchard is about 24.7 acres. A city park of 2.5 ha is roughly 6.2 acres—useful on bilingual trail signs."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:57
msgid "A 10-foot shipping container width constraint is 3.048 m—container specs are often written both ways. A 6 ft person is 1.83 m, the figure hospitals and passport forms outside the US usually expect."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:93
msgid "A 10-yard fabric bolt section is 9.144 m—enough to plan metric pattern layouts. A first-down marker at 10 yards is 9.14 m on a metric practice field overlay."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:379
msgid "A 100 km/h highway limit is about 62 mph. A city 50 km/h zone is roughly 31 mph—close to many US 30 mph neighborhood limits."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:87
msgid "A 100 m dash is about 109.4 yards. Ordering 3 m of upholstery fabric means about 3.28 yards; round up if the bolt is sold in whole yards only."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:51
msgid "A 12 m yacht length overall is about 39.4 feet for marina berth booking in the US. A 3 m sofa wall needs roughly 9.8 feet of clear space—buyers often round up to 10 feet when shopping."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:323
msgid "A 12 oz steak is about 340 g—handy for metric doneness charts per centimetre thickness. First-class mail at 3.5 oz is about 99 g."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:267
msgid "A 18 ft³ refrigerator is about 510 L—compare to European fridge labels in litres. A 2 ft³ minifridge is roughly 56.6 L of internal volume."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:311
msgid "A 180 lb adult is about 81.6 kg on a metric chart. A 40 lb bag of dog food is roughly 18.1 kg for shelves labeled only in kilograms."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:341
msgid "A 2 t palletized load is about 4,409 lb—check a forklift rated in pounds. A 0.5 t delivery is roughly 1,102 lb for a US pickup payload chart."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:297
msgid "A 2,500 L bright tank is 25 hL on a production schedule. Milk intake of 12,000 L in a morning is 120 hL for a co-op report."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:217
msgid "A 2,500 m² community garden is 0.25 ha. A 40,000 m² warehouse yard is 4 ha—handy for logistics land-use filings."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:453
msgid "A 2.25-hour seminar is 135 minutes. Slow-cooking for 8 hours is 480 minutes on a device that only accepts minutes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:825
msgid "A 2.5-acre hobby farm is about 1.01 ha or about 10 117 m². A 40-hectare orchard is 0.4 km² and about 98.8 acres. These ballparks help when reading international listings."
msgstr "Une ferme d'agrément de 2,5 acres fait environ 1,01 ha ou environ 10 117 m². Un verger de 40 hectares fait 0,4 km² et environ 98,8 acres. Ces approximations aident lors de la lecture des listes internationales."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:27
msgid "A 2×4 stud is nominally 1.5 inches thick, which is 3.81 cm—useful when a metric drywall screw pack lists max material thickness in centimetres. A 55-inch TV diagonal is 139.7 cm for checking elevator and doorway clearance."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:415
msgid "A 20-knot wind is 37 km/h—near a strong breeze on land-based km/h apps. A ship cruising at 15 kn makes about 27.8 km/h over water."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:273
msgid "A 200 L chest freezer is about 7.06 ft³ on US retail tags. A 1000 L IBC tote is roughly 35.3 ft³ for warehouse slot planning."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:305
msgid "A 23 kg airline allowance is about 50.7 lb—just over a common 50 lb US checked-bag limit. A 100 kg barbell is roughly 220.5 lb on a US plate math board."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:317
msgid "A 250 g coffee bag is about 8.82 oz—near a common 8 oz retail size after rounding. A 28 g protein snack is essentially 1 oz."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:237
msgid "A 3 m³ water delivery is 3,000 L—about sixty 50 L barrels. An aquarium billed as 0.36 m³ is a 360 L tank in hobby shop language."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:465
msgid "A 3-day courier promise is 72 hours if counted continuously. A 10-day medication course is 240 hours of coverage at face value."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:441
msgid "A 3-minute plank hold is 180 seconds on a phone timer. Developing film for 7.5 minutes means 450 seconds on a metronome-style process clock."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:347
msgid "A 4,400 lb machine is about 2.00 t for a metric bill of lading. A 500 lb crate is roughly 0.227 t (227 kg)—often better written in kilograms on the same form."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:205
msgid "A 4×6 inch photo is 24 in², about 155 cm² of print area. A 1 in² ventilation hole is 6.45 cm² for metric airflow notes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:181
msgid "A 40-acre parcel is about 16.2 hectares—common quarter-quarter section talk in metric reports. A 5-acre hobby farm is roughly 2.02 ha for EU subsidy forms."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:63
msgid "A 42.195 km marathon is 26.219 miles—the classic race distance. A 120 km drive is about 74.6 miles; at 8 L/100 km that trip burns roughly the same fuel as about 29.4 mpg over those miles."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:111
msgid "A 5-yard pass play covers 15 feet of field. Buying 4 yards of landscape fabric means 12 feet of linear run along a bed edge."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:99
msgid "A 5,000 m training interval is a 5 km workout. A 42,195 m race distance is the marathon’s 42.195 km official length."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:211
msgid "A 50 cm² adhesive patch is about 7.75 in²—compare to US first-aid box labels. A business card near 46 cm² is roughly 7.1 in²."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:231
msgid "A 500 L rain barrel is 0.5 m³. A small pool holding 25,000 L is 25 m³ for chemical dosing charts that use grams per m³."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:365
msgid "A 500 mg pain tablet is 0.5 g of drug substance labeled strength. Caffeine at 80 mg in espresso is 0.08 g—useful when a lab protocol wants grams."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1466
msgid "A 5K is five kilometres (about 3.1 miles). Always read the K as kilometres in race names."
msgstr "Un 5K fait cinq kilomètres (environ 3,1 miles). Lisez toujours le K en kilomètres dans les noms de courses."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:81
msgid "A 6 ft 1 in doorway rough opening is 185.4 cm—compare that to a 200 cm metric door slab with trim. A 5-foot Christmas tree is 152.4 cm for European height labels."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:477
msgid "A 6-week physiotherapy program is 42 days. A 2-week vacation hold is 14 days of uninterrupted leave if using calendar days."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:169
msgid "A 75 m² flat is about 807 sq ft—typical one-bedroom sizing talk in US cities. Ordering vinyl for 20 m² means roughly 215 sq ft; add waste percentage after converting."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:353
msgid "A 750 g loaf is 0.75 kg. Buying 2,500 g of flour is a 2.5 kg bag—standard supermarket sizing."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:243
msgid "A 750 mL wine bottle is 0.75 L. A 5 mL medicine teaspoon is 0.005 L—useful when a protocol lists litres only."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:105
msgid "A 8.5-foot counter run is 102 inches for a continuous laminate order. Someone 5.75 feet tall is 69 inches on a medical form that only accepts inches."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:157
msgid "A barleycorn is an old English length unit equal to one-third of an inch. It historically underpinned shoe sizing systems."
msgstr "Un grain d'orge est une ancienne unité de longueur anglaise égale à un tiers de pouce. Historiquement, il sous-tend les systèmes de pointure des chaussures."

#: src/lib/units.ts:530
msgid "A barn (b) equals 10⁻²⁸ square metres. Particle physicists use it as a convenient unit for nuclear and particle interaction cross-sections."
msgstr "Une grange (b) équivaut à 10⁻²⁸ mètres carrés. Les physiciens des particules l'utilisent comme unité pratique pour les sections efficaces d'interaction nucléaire et particulaire."

#: src/lib/units.ts:695
msgid "A board (board measure area) equals about 0.00774 square metres—the face area of a one-inch by one-foot board. Lumber trades use related board measures."
msgstr "Une planche (surface de mesure de la planche) équivaut à environ 0,00774 mètres carrés, soit la surface frontale d'une planche d'un pouce sur un pied. Les métiers du bois utilisent des mesures de conseil connexes."

#: src/lib/units.ts:883
msgid "A board foot is a lumber volume of 1 foot × 1 foot × 1 inch, about 2.36 litres. Softwood and hardwood trades price wood by board feet."
msgstr "Un pied-planche est un volume de bois de 1 pied × 1 pied × 1 pouce, soit environ 2,36 litres. Les métiers du bois résineux et feuillu évaluent le bois en pieds-planche."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:291
msgid "A brewery making 50 hL per batch produces 5,000 L—about 88 half-hectolitre kegs depending on keg size. A 2 hL fermenter is a 200 L vessel."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:864
msgid "A Brief History of Temperature Scales"
msgstr "Une brève histoire des échelles de température"

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:137
msgid "A candy thermometer reading of 300 °F is about 149 °C for soft-crack stage in metric candy charts. Weather at 68 °F is 20 °C—handy when packing for a city that posts only Celsius."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:828
msgid "A centilitre (cL) equals 10 millilitres. Beverage packaging in Europe often labels volume in centilitres."
msgstr "Un centilitre (cL) équivaut à 10 millilitres. En Europe, les emballages de boissons indiquent souvent le volume en centilitres."

#: src/lib/units.ts:168
msgid "A centimetre (cm) equals 0.01 metres. It is one of the most familiar metric units for body measurements, clothing, and school science."
msgstr "Un centimètre (cm) équivaut à 0,01 mètre. C’est l’une des unités métriques les plus connues pour les mesures corporelles, les vêtements et les sciences scolaires."

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:225
msgid "A centimetre per second (cm/s) equals 0.01 metres per second. Laboratory flow rates and slow mechanical motions are often expressed in cm/s."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:613
msgid "A checklist before you convert"
msgstr "Une liste de contrôle avant de vous convertir"

#: src/lib/units.ts:706
msgid "A circular inch is the area of a circle one inch in diameter, about 0.785 square inches. Wire and tubing sizing historically used circular measures."
msgstr "Un pouce circulaire est l'aire d'un cercle d'un pouce de diamètre, soit environ 0,785 pouce carré. Le dimensionnement des fils et des tubes utilisait historiquement des mesures circulaires."

#: src/lib/units.ts:717
msgid "A circular mil is the area of a circle 0.001 inch in diameter. Electrical engineering uses it to specify wire cross-sectional area."
msgstr "Un mil circulaire est l’aire d’un cercle de 0,001 pouce de diamètre. L'ingénierie électrique l'utilise pour spécifier la section transversale des fils."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:639
msgid "A clear explanation of the light-year as a length unit—how it relates to metres, why astronomy uses it, and how it compares to AUs and parsecs."
msgstr "Une explication claire de l'année-lumière en tant qu'unité de longueur : comment elle se rapporte aux mètres, pourquoi l'astronomie l'utilise et comment elle se compare aux UA et aux parsecs."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:414
msgid "A clear tour of SI prefixes—milli, centi, kilo, mega, nano, and more—so you can scale length, area, and volume without losing track of powers of ten."
msgstr "Une présentation claire des préfixes SI (milli, centi, kilo, méga, nano et plus encore) afin que vous puissiez redimensionner la longueur, la surface et le volume sans perdre la trace des puissances de dix."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:128
msgid "A coherent system picks one base for each quantity. For length, SI uses the metre. Feet, miles, nanometres, and light-years can all be expressed as a multiple of metres. For area, the coherent SI unit is the square metre; for volume, the cubic metre. Litres are convenient but still defined through cubic metres."
msgstr "Un système cohérent choisit une base pour chaque quantité. Pour la longueur, SI utilise le mètre. Les pieds, les miles, les nanomètres et les années-lumière peuvent tous être exprimés sous la forme d'un multiple de mètres. Pour la surface, l'unité cohérente SI est le mètre carré ; pour le volume, le mètre cube. Les litres sont pratiques mais toujours définis en mètres cubes."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:120
msgid "A conversion factor is a ratio equal to 1 that changes the unit label without changing the physical quantity. Writing 1 in = 2.54 cm means the fraction (2.54 cm)/(1 in) equals one. Multiply a measurement by that fraction and the inches cancel, leaving centimetres."
msgstr "Un facteur de conversion est un rapport égal à 1 qui modifie l'étiquette de l'unité sans changer la quantité physique. Écrire 1 po = 2,54 cm signifie que la fraction (2,54 cm)/(1 po) est égale à un. Multipliez une mesure par cette fraction et les pouces s'annulent, laissant des centimètres."

#: src/lib/units.ts:817
msgid "A cubic centimetre (cm³ or cc) equals one millilitre. Medicine and engine displacement commonly use this name."
msgstr "Un centimètre cube (cm³ ou cc) équivaut à un millilitre. La médecine et la cylindrée du moteur utilisent couramment ce nom."

#: src/lib/units.ts:894
msgid "A cubic decimetre (dm³) equals exactly one litre. SI texts often prefer this name when emphasizing volume as length cubed."
msgstr "Un décimètre cube (dm³) équivaut exactement à un litre. Les textes SI préfèrent souvent ce nom lorsqu'ils mettent l'accent sur le volume comme longueur au cube."

#: src/lib/units.ts:905
msgid "A cubic dekametre (dam³) equals 1,000 cubic metres. Large civil-engineering and water volumes may use this SI multiple."
msgstr "Un décamètre cube (dam³) équivaut à 1 000 mètres cubes. De grands volumes de génie civil et d’eau peuvent utiliser ce multiple SI."

#: src/lib/units.ts:916
msgid "A cubic fathom equals about 6.12 cubic metres. Historical maritime cargo and dredging contexts used cubic fathoms."
msgstr "Une brasse cube équivaut à environ 6,12 mètres cubes. Les contextes historiques de fret maritime et de dragage utilisaient des brasses cubes."

#: src/lib/units.ts:927
msgid "A cubic foot equals about 28.3 litres. HVAC, shipping, and US construction routinely measure volume in cubic feet."
msgstr "Un pied cube équivaut à environ 28,3 litres. Les secteurs du CVC, du transport maritime et de la construction aux États-Unis mesurent régulièrement le volume en pieds cubes."

#: src/lib/units.ts:938
msgid "A cubic hectometre (hm³) equals one million cubic metres. Reservoir capacity and river discharge are often quoted in hm³."
msgstr "Un hectomètre cube (hm³) équivaut à un million de mètres cubes. La capacité des réservoirs et le débit des rivières sont souvent indiqués en hm³."

#: src/lib/units.ts:949
msgid "A cubic inch equals about 16.4 millilitres. Engine displacement in the US was long advertised in cubic inches."
msgstr "Un pouce cube équivaut à environ 16,4 millilitres. Aux États-Unis, la cylindrée du moteur a longtemps été annoncée en pouces cubes."

#: src/lib/units.ts:960
msgid "A cubic kilometre (km³) equals one billion cubic metres. Geology and oceanography use it for enormous natural volumes."
msgstr "Un kilomètre cube (km³) équivaut à un milliard de mètres cubes. La géologie et l'océanographie l'utilisent pour d'énormes volumes naturels."

#: src/lib/units.ts:740
msgid "A cubic micrometre (µm³) equals 10⁻¹⁸ cubic metres. Cell biology and microparticle work often report volumes this way."
msgstr "Un micromètre cube (µm³) équivaut à 10⁻¹⁸ mètres cubes. La biologie cellulaire et les travaux sur les microparticules rapportent souvent des volumes de cette façon."

#: src/lib/units.ts:982
msgid "A cubic mile equals about 4.17 cubic kilometres. Large natural features such as aquifers or ice sheets may be described in cubic miles."
msgstr "Un mile cube équivaut à environ 4,17 kilomètres cubes. Les grands éléments naturels tels que les aquifères ou les calottes glaciaires peuvent être décrits en miles cubes."

#: src/lib/units.ts:784
msgid "A cubic millimetre (mm³) equals one microlitre. Medicine and engineering use it for small solid or fluid volumes."
msgstr "Un millimètre cube (mm³) équivaut à un microlitre. La médecine et l'ingénierie l'utilisent pour de petits volumes solides ou fluides."

#: src/lib/units.ts:729
msgid "A cubic nanometre (nm³) equals 10⁻²⁷ cubic metres. It describes molecular-scale volumes in nanoscience."
msgstr "Un nanomètre cube (nm³) équivaut à 10⁻²⁷ mètres cubes. Il décrit les volumes à l'échelle moléculaire en nanoscience."

#: src/lib/units.ts:993
msgid "A cubic yard equals about 0.765 cubic metres. Construction and landscaping in the US buy concrete, soil, and mulch by the cubic yard."
msgstr "Un mètre cube équivaut à environ 0,765 mètre cube. Aux États-Unis, la construction et l’aménagement paysager achètent du béton, de la terre et du paillis au mètre cube."

#: src/lib/units.ts:212
msgid "A cubit is an ancient length unit based on the forearm, standardized here at 0.4572 metres. It appears in historical architecture and biblical scholarship."
msgstr "La coudée est une ancienne unité de longueur basée sur l'avant-bras, standardisée ici à 0,4572 mètres. Il apparaît dans l'architecture historique et l'érudition biblique."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2076
msgid "A cup of flour can vary by tens of grams depending on scooping and humidity. A 120 g portion does not. Grams and ounces measure mass; cups measure volume. When a recipe lists weight, trust the scale and convert units—do not re-approximate with cups unless you accept variability."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:33
msgid "A curtain drop of 84 inches is 7 feet exactly—standard floor-length drapery. A workbench at 36 inches high is 3 feet, matching many metric 900 mm benches within a few millimetres."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:314
msgid "A day equals 86,400 seconds (24 hours). Calendars and daily planning treat the mean solar day as the basic civil time unit."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:267
msgid "A decametre (dam) equals 10 metres. It is an SI multiple occasionally used for surveying and athletics track distances."
msgstr "Un décamètre (barrage) équivaut à 10 mètres. Il s'agit d'un multiple SI parfois utilisé pour l'arpentage et les distances sur piste d'athlétisme."

#: src/lib/units.ts:839
msgid "A decilitre (dL) equals 100 millilitres. Cooking and nutrition labels in some countries use decilitres."
msgstr "Un décilitre (dL) équivaut à 100 millilitres. Dans certains pays, les étiquettes culinaires et nutritionnelles utilisent des décilitres."

#: src/lib/units.ts:190
msgid "A decimetre (dm) equals 0.1 metres, or 10 centimetres. It appears in metric education and some industrial specifications."
msgstr "Un décimètre (dm) équivaut à 0,1 mètre, soit 10 centimètres. Il apparaît dans l'enseignement métrique et dans certaines spécifications industrielles."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:271
msgid "A degree Celsius and a kelvin are the same size. That is why converting Celsius to Kelvin is addition: T(K) = t(°C) + 273.15. Fahrenheit degrees are smaller: one Fahrenheit degree is 5/9 of a Celsius degree."
msgstr "Un degré Celsius et un kelvin ont la même taille. C'est pourquoi la conversion de Celsius en Kelvin est une addition : T(K) = t(°C) + 273,15. Les degrés Fahrenheit sont plus petits : un degré Fahrenheit équivaut à 5/9 de degré Celsius."

#: src/lib/units.ts:1015
msgid "A dekalitre (daL) equals 10 litres. Beverage and agricultural bulk liquids sometimes use dekalitres."
msgstr "Un décalitre (daL) équivaut à 10 litres. Les boissons et les liquides agricoles en vrac utilisent parfois des décalitres."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:161
msgid "A detector cooled to 77 K is about −321 °F—colder than dry ice (−109 °F). Human skin temperature ~306 K is about 91 °F, matching infrared thermometer expectations."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:256
msgid "A fathom equals 1.8288 metres (6 feet). Mariners traditionally use it to express water depth."
msgstr "Une brasse équivaut à 1,8288 mètres (6 pieds). Les marins l'utilisent traditionnellement pour exprimer la profondeur de l'eau."

#: src/lib/units.ts:74
msgid "A femtometre (fm), also called a fermi, equals 10⁻¹⁵ metres. Nuclear physicists use it to measure the size of atomic nuclei and nucleons."
msgstr "Un femtomètre (fm), également appelé fermi, équivaut à 10⁻¹⁵ mètres. Les physiciens nucléaires l'utilisent pour mesurer la taille des noyaux atomiques et des nucléons."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1065
msgid "A field checklist"
msgstr "Une liste de contrôle sur le terrain"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2325
msgid "A flight that leaves at 17:00 and lands at 19:00 local at the destination may last 8–12 hours depending on zones. Always trust block time (a duration) from the airline for “how long you sit,” and local times for “when to be at the gate.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:201
msgid "A foot per second (ft/s) equals exactly 0.3048 metres per second. Engineering, ballistics, and some US technical contexts use feet per second."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:391
msgid "A gale at 20 m/s is 72 km/h. A sprinter near 10 m/s peaks around 36 km/h—useful when comparing to traffic speeds."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:355
msgid "A gigametre (Gm) equals one billion metres. Astronomers sometimes use it for distances within the inner Solar System."
msgstr "Un gigamètre (Gm) équivaut à un milliard de mètres. Les astronomes l'utilisent parfois pour mesurer les distances à l'intérieur du système solaire interne."

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:152
msgid "A grain equals exactly 0.00006479891 kilograms. Historically based on a grain of cereal, it still appears in ammunition, archery, and precious-metal weighing."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:56
msgid "A gram (g) equals one thousandth of a kilogram. It is the familiar metric unit for kitchen scales, nutrition labels, and small packages."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:488
msgid "A Gregorian mean year is 365.2425 days—close but not identical to 365.25. Calendar age in birthdays is not Julian-year duration. Leap-second tables affect civil time, not the Julian-year day count definition used here."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:223
msgid "A half-acre suburban lot is about 2,023 m². A 10-acre solar field offers roughly 40,469 m² of land before setbacks and roads."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:662
msgid "A hectare (ha) equals 10,000 square metres (100 ares). Agriculture and land management worldwide report field sizes in hectares."
msgstr "Un hectare (ha) équivaut à 10 000 mètres carrés (100 ares). L’agriculture et la gestion des terres dans le monde indiquent la taille des champs en hectares."

#: src/lib/units.ts:1026
msgid "A hectolitre (hL) equals 100 litres. Brewing, wine production, and grain trade historically favour hectolitres."
msgstr "Un hectolitre (hL) équivaut à 100 litres. La brasserie, la production de vin et le commerce des céréales privilégient historiquement les hectolitres."

#: src/lib/units.ts:289
msgid "A hectometre (hm) equals 100 metres. It is an SI multiple used in meteorology (rainfall rates) and some sports distances."
msgstr "Un hectomètre (hm) équivaut à 100 mètres. C'est un multiple SI utilisé en météorologie (taux de précipitations) et dans certaines distances sportives."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:75
msgid "A height of 175 cm is 5.74 feet, usually spoken as 5 ft 9 in. A 240 cm curtain fabric cut is 7.87 feet—order 8 feet of material if the shop sells by the foot."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:433
msgid "A human hair is on the order of tens of micrometres. Visible light wavelengths sit around hundreds of nanometres. Atomic spacings are on the order of tenths of a nanometre (ångströms). Road distances use kilometres; machining uses millimetres; optics and semiconductors live in micrometres and nanometres."
msgstr "Un cheveu humain mesure de l'ordre de quelques dizaines de micromètres. Les longueurs d’onde de la lumière visible se situent autour de centaines de nanomètres. Les espacements atomiques sont de l'ordre du dixième de nanomètre (ångströms). Les distances routières utilisent les kilomètres ; l'usinage utilise des millimètres ; l'optique et les semi-conducteurs vivent dans les micromètres et les nanomètres."

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:338
msgid "A Julian year equals exactly 365.25 mean solar days (31,557,600 seconds). Astronomy uses the Julian year as a fixed long-duration time unit."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:155
msgid "A kiln note of 1800 °F is about 1255 K—useful when a ceramics paper cites peak temperature in kelvin. Room temperature ~70 °F is roughly 294 K for electronics thermal margins."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:311
msgid "A kilometre (km) equals 1,000 metres. It is the standard metric unit for road distances, maps, and athletic races."
msgstr "Un kilomètre (km) équivaut à 1 000 mètres. Il s'agit de l'unité métrique standard pour les distances routières, les cartes et les courses sportives."

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:177
msgid "A kilometre per hour (km/h) equals one kilometre of travel in one hour, or exactly 1/3.6 metres per second. Road signs worldwide display vehicle speed in km/h."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1774
msgid "A knot is a nautical mile per hour"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:213
msgid "A knot is one international nautical mile per hour, equal to 1852/3600 metres per second. Aviation and maritime navigation report speed in knots."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:762
msgid "A lambda (λ) is a laboratory volume unit equal to one microlitre (10⁻⁶ L). Older biochemistry literature still uses the name."
msgstr "Un lambda (λ) est une unité de volume de laboratoire égale à un microlitre (10⁻⁶ L). La littérature biochimique plus ancienne utilise encore ce nom."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:21
msgid "A laptop listed as 35.6 cm wide is 14 inches (35.6 ÷ 2.54). A European jeans waist of 81 cm is about 31.9 inches—close enough to pick a US size 32, then confirm the brand’s size chart."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:410
msgid "A light-day is the distance light travels in one day, about 26 trillion metres. It bridges Solar System and nearby interstellar scales."
msgstr "Un jour-lumière est la distance parcourue par la lumière en une journée, soit environ 26 000 milliards de mètres. Il relie le système solaire et les échelles interstellaires proches."

#: src/lib/units.ts:399
msgid "A light-hour is the distance light travels in one hour, about 1.079 billion kilometres. It spans distances comparable to the outer planets' orbits."
msgstr "Une heure-lumière correspond à la distance parcourue par la lumière en une heure, soit environ 1,079 milliard de kilomètres. Il s'étend sur des distances comparables aux orbites des planètes extérieures."

#: src/lib/units.ts:377
msgid "A light-minute is the distance light travels in one minute, about 18 million kilometres. The Sun–Earth light time is roughly eight light-minutes."
msgstr "Une minute-lumière correspond à la distance parcourue par la lumière en une minute, soit environ 18 millions de kilomètres. Le temps d’éclairage Soleil-Terre est d’environ huit minutes-lumière."

#: src/lib/units.ts:366
msgid "A light-second is the distance light travels in one second in vacuum, exactly 299,792,458 metres. It helps express near-Earth space distances."
msgstr "Une seconde-lumière correspond à la distance parcourue par la lumière en une seconde dans le vide, soit exactement 299 792 458 mètres. Il permet d'exprimer les distances spatiales proches de la Terre."

#: src/lib/units.ts:421
msgid "A light-year (ly) is the distance light travels in one Julian year, about 9.46 trillion kilometres. It is the most familiar unit for interstellar distances."
msgstr "Une année-lumière (ly) est la distance parcourue par la lumière en une année julienne, soit environ 9,46 billions de kilomètres. C'est l'unité la plus connue pour les distances interstellaires."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:122
msgid "A light-year is distance, not time—do not treat “4 years” as the converted value. Parsecs and astronomical units are different; convert ly→km, do not mix AU factors casually. Rounding to “9.5 trillion km” is fine for talk, not for precise ephemerides."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:650
msgid "A light-year is the distance light travels in vacuum in one Julian year. Despite the word year, it is a length unit, not a time unit. Saying a star is 4 light-years away means its light takes about four years to reach us—and that the path length is that many light-years."
msgstr "Une année-lumière est la distance parcourue par la lumière dans le vide en une année julienne. Malgré le mot année, il s’agit d’une unité de longueur et non d’une unité de temps. Dire qu’une étoile est à 4 années-lumière signifie que sa lumière met environ quatre ans pour nous atteindre – et que la longueur du trajet est de autant d’années-lumière."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:648
msgid "A light-year measures distance"
msgstr "Une année-lumière mesure la distance"

#: src/lib/units.ts:1048
msgid "A litre (L) equals 0.001 cubic metres. It is the everyday metric unit for beverages, fuel, and household liquids."
msgstr "Un litre (L) équivaut à 0,001 mètre cube. C'est l'unité métrique courante pour les boissons, les carburants et les liquides ménagers."

#: src/lib/units.ts:344
msgid "A megametre (Mm) equals one million metres (1,000 kilometres). It is useful for planetary-scale distances."
msgstr "Un mégamètre (Mm) équivaut à un million de mètres (1 000 kilomètres). C’est utile pour les distances à l’échelle planétaire."

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:140
msgid "A metric carat equals exactly 0.0002 kilograms (200 milligrams). Jewellers use carats to express the mass of gemstones such as diamonds."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:1004
msgid "A metric cup is standardized here as 250 millilitres. Cooking recipes use cups for everyday liquid and dry measures."
msgstr "Une tasse métrique est standardisée ici à 250 millilitres. Les recettes de cuisine utilisent des tasses pour les mesures quotidiennes de liquides et de matières sèches."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:358
msgid "A metric cup of 250 mL is one-quarter of a litre. Sixteen US tablespoons make a US cup in customary cooking arithmetic, but verify against millilitres when converting a metric recipe. When in doubt, convert everything to millilitres first, then back to the utensil you own."
msgstr "Une tasse métrique de 250 ml équivaut à un quart de litre. Seize cuillères à soupe américaines donnent une tasse américaine en arithmétique culinaire habituelle, mais comparez-les aux millilitres lors de la conversion d'une recette métrique. En cas de doute, convertissez d'abord tout en millilitres, puis revenez à l'ustensile que vous possédez."

#: src/lib/units.ts:795
msgid "A metric drop is standardized here as 50 microlitres. Pharmacy and laboratory instructions sometimes dose liquids by drops."
msgstr "Une goutte métrique est standardisée ici à 50 microlitres. Les instructions en pharmacie et en laboratoire dosent parfois les liquides au compte-gouttes."

#: src/lib/units.ts:1037
msgid "A metric tablespoon equals 15 millilitres. Cooking instructions use it for medium liquid and condiment measures."
msgstr "Une cuillère à soupe métrique équivaut à 15 millilitres. Instructions de cuisson : utilisez-le pour les mesures moyennes de liquide et de condiments."

#: src/lib/units.ts:850
msgid "A metric teaspoon equals 5 millilitres. Cooking recipes use it for small liquid and powder measures."
msgstr "Une cuillère à café métrique équivaut à 5 millilitres. Les recettes de cuisine l'utilisent pour les petites mesures de liquides et de poudre."

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:92
msgid "A metric tonne (t) equals 1,000 kilograms. Industry, shipping, and agriculture use tonnes for bulk cargo and large loads."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:80
msgid "A microgram (µg) equals one billionth of a kilogram (10⁻⁹ kg). Trace nutrients, pollutants, and sensitive analytical chemistry use micrograms."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:773
msgid "A microlitre (µL) equals one millionth of a litre. Pipettes in biology and chemistry routinely dispense microlitre volumes."
msgstr "Un microlitre (µL) équivaut à un millionième de litre. Les pipettes en biologie et en chimie distribuent régulièrement des volumes de microlitres."

#: src/lib/units.ts:135
msgid "A micrometre (µm), or micron, equals 10⁻⁶ metres. Biologists use it for cell sizes; engineers use it for fine manufacturing tolerances."
msgstr "Un micromètre (µm), ou micron, équivaut à 10⁻⁶ mètres. Les biologistes l'utilisent pour déterminer la taille des cellules ; les ingénieurs l'utilisent pour des tolérances de fabrication fines."

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:266
msgid "A microsecond (µs) equals one millionth of a second (10⁻⁶ s). High-speed electronics and scientific instrumentation resolve events in microseconds."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:68
msgid "A milligram (mg) equals one millionth of a kilogram (10⁻⁶ kg). Medicine doses and laboratory samples are often measured in milligrams."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:806
msgid "A millilitre (mL) equals one cubic centimetre. Medicine, cooking, and laboratory work use millilitres for precise liquid volumes."
msgstr "Un millilitre (mL) équivaut à un centimètre cube. La médecine, la cuisine et les travaux de laboratoire utilisent des millilitres pour des volumes de liquide précis."

#: src/lib/units.ts:146
msgid "A millimetre (mm) equals 0.001 metres. It is a common everyday metric unit for small objects, engineering drawings, and rainfall."
msgstr "Un millimètre (mm) équivaut à 0,001 mètre. Il s'agit d'une unité métrique courante pour les petits objets, les dessins techniques et les précipitations."

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:254
msgid "A millisecond (ms) equals one thousandth of a second. Computing latency, photography shutter speeds, and sports timing often use milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:290
msgid "A minute equals 60 seconds. Everyday schedules, cooking, and sports use minutes as a convenient subdivision of the hour."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:124
msgid "A nanometre (nm) equals one billionth of a metre (10⁻⁹ m). It is the everyday unit for wavelengths of light, nanotechnology, and thin films."
msgstr "Un nanomètre (nm) équivaut à un milliardième de mètre (10⁻⁹ m). C'est l'unité courante pour les longueurs d'onde de la lumière, la nanotechnologie et les couches minces."

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:278
msgid "A nanosecond (ns) equals one billionth of a second (10⁻⁹ s). Computer clock cycles and light travel over short distances are measured in nanoseconds."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1697
msgid "A number on a white sign means nothing until you know whether it is mph or km/h. Driving 100 in a 100 km/h zone is not the same as driving 100 in a 100 mph zone—the second case is roughly 161 km/h. Tourists who “just match the number” cause genuine danger."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:432
msgid "A parsec (pc) equals about 3.26 light-years. Astronomers prefer it because it relates directly to stellar parallax measurements."
msgstr "Un parsec (pc) équivaut à environ 3,26 années-lumière. Les astronomes le préfèrent car il est directement lié aux mesures de parallaxe stellaire."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:707
msgid "A parsec is larger—about 3.26 light-years. Professional astronomy often prefers parsecs; outreach often prefers light-years."
msgstr "Un parsec est plus grand : environ 3,26 années-lumière. L'astronomie professionnelle préfère souvent les parsecs ; la sensibilisation préfère souvent les années-lumière."

#: src/lib/units.ts:751
msgid "A picolitre (pL) equals 10⁻¹² litres. Microfluidics and inkjet printing deal with volumes at this scale."
msgstr "Un picolitre (pL) équivaut à 10⁻¹² litres. La microfluidique et l’impression jet d’encre traitent des volumes à cette échelle."

#: src/lib/units.ts:85
msgid "A picometre (pm) equals 10⁻¹² metres. It is commonly used for atomic radii and bond lengths in chemistry."
msgstr "Un picomètre (pm) équivaut à 10⁻¹² mètres. Il est couramment utilisé pour les rayons atomiques et les longueurs de liaison en chimie."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:34
msgid "A practical comparison of metric and imperial units for length, volume, and area—when each system wins and how to convert between them confidently."
msgstr "Une comparaison pratique des unités métriques et impériales pour la longueur, le volume et la surface : quand chaque système gagne et comment convertir entre eux en toute confiance."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:973
msgid "A practical conversion strategy"
msgstr "Une stratégie de conversion pratique"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1166
msgid "A practical decision guide for picking length, area, volume, and temperature units that keep numbers readable, standards-compliant, and hard to misinterpret."
msgstr "Un guide de décision pratique pour choisir des unités de longueur, de surface, de volume et de température qui maintiennent les chiffres lisibles, conformes aux normes et difficiles à mal interpréter."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1577
msgid "A reliable conversion workflow"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:387
msgid "A reliable workflow for converting any recipe"
msgstr "Un flux de travail fiable pour convertir n'importe quelle recette"

#: src/lib/units.ts:489
msgid "A scale and unit of measurement for temperature used by most of the world."
msgstr "Échelle et unité de mesure de la température utilisées dans la plupart des pays du monde."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1027
msgid "A shaft specified as 10.00 ± 0.02 mm is not the same as casually writing 0.394 in after a phone conversion rounded to three decimals. Soft conversion can eat the tolerance budget before the machine starts. The scrap bin fills with parts that were converted casually rather than machined poorly."
msgstr "Un axe spécifié comme 10,00 ± 0,02 mm n'est pas la même chose que d'écrire négligemment 0,394 po après une conversion téléphonique arrondie à trois décimales. La conversion douce peut consommer le budget de tolérance avant le démarrage de la machine. Le bac à ferraille se remplit de pièces qui ont été transformées avec désinvolture plutôt que mal usinées."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1215
msgid "A short decision recipe"
msgstr "Une courte recette de décision"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1392
msgid "A simple baking workflow"
msgstr "Un flux de travail de cuisson simple"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:169
msgid "A single base keeps every unit definition consistent and reduces the number of stored factors. Direct factors are fine when you trust them; the base-unit path is the reliable pattern for software and for checking hand calculations."
msgstr "Une base unique maintient la cohérence de chaque définition d'unité et réduit le nombre de facteurs stockés. Les facteurs directs sont acceptables lorsque vous leur faites confiance ; le chemin de l'unité de base est le modèle fiable pour les logiciels et pour vérifier les calculs manuels."

#: src/lib/units.ts:574
msgid "A square centimetre (cm²) equals 10⁻⁴ square metres. It is a familiar school and laboratory unit for small surfaces."
msgstr "Un centimètre carré (cm²) équivaut à 10⁻⁴ mètres carrés. C'est une unité d'école et de laboratoire familière pour les petites surfaces."

#: src/lib/units.ts:596
msgid "A square decimetre (dm²) equals 0.01 square metres. It sits between the centimetre and metre squared in the metric area ladder."
msgstr "Un décimètre carré (dm²) équivaut à 0,01 mètre carré. Il se situe entre le centimètre et le mètre carré dans l’échelle métrique."

#: src/lib/units.ts:607
msgid "A square foot equals about 0.0929 square metres. Real estate, flooring, and construction in the US routinely use square feet."
msgstr "Un pied carré équivaut à environ 0,0929 mètres carrés. Aux États-Unis, l'immobilier, les revêtements de sol et la construction utilisent régulièrement des pieds carrés."

#: src/lib/units.ts:585
msgid "A square inch equals 645.16 square millimetres. US customary technical drawings and packaging often specify area in square inches."
msgstr "Un pouce carré équivaut à 645,16 millimètres carrés. Les dessins techniques et les emballages habituels aux États-Unis spécifient souvent la superficie en pouces carrés."

#: src/lib/units.ts:673
msgid "A square kilometre (km²) equals one million square metres. Maps and geography use it for cities, regions, and countries."
msgstr "Un kilomètre carré (km²) équivaut à un million de mètres carrés. Les cartes et la géographie l'utilisent pour les villes, les régions et les pays."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:441
msgid "A square kilometre is not 10³ square metres—it is (10³)² = 10⁶ square metres. A cubic centimetre is (10⁻²)³ = 10⁻⁶ cubic metres. Forgetting to square or cube the prefix power is the classic SI scaling mistake."
msgstr "Un kilomètre carré ne fait pas 10³ mètres carrés, c'est (10³)² = 10⁶ mètres carrés. Un centimètre cube équivaut à (10⁻²)³ = 10⁻⁶ mètres cubes. Oublier de mettre au carré ou au cube la puissance du préfixe est l'erreur classique de mise à l'échelle SI."

#: src/lib/units.ts:552
msgid "A square micrometre (µm²) equals 10⁻¹² square metres. Microscopy and microfabrication often report areas in this unit."
msgstr "Un micromètre carré (µm²) équivaut à 10⁻¹² mètres carrés. La microscopie et la microfabrication signalent souvent des zones dans cette unité."

#: src/lib/units.ts:684
msgid "A square mile equals about 2.59 square kilometres. US and UK geographic statistics often express large areas in square miles."
msgstr "Un mile carré équivaut à environ 2,59 kilomètres carrés. Les statistiques géographiques des États-Unis et du Royaume-Uni expriment souvent de vastes zones en miles carrés."

#: src/lib/units.ts:563
msgid "A square millimetre (mm²) equals 10⁻⁶ square metres. Engineering drawings and small-component cross-sections commonly use it."
msgstr "Un millimètre carré (mm²) équivaut à 10⁻⁶ mètres carrés. Les dessins techniques et les coupes transversales de petits composants l'utilisent couramment."

#: src/lib/units.ts:541
msgid "A square nanometre (nm²) equals 10⁻¹⁸ square metres. It measures ultra-small surface areas in nanotechnology and materials science."
msgstr "Un nanomètre carré (nm²) équivaut à 10⁻¹⁸ mètres carrés. Il mesure des surfaces ultra-petites en nanotechnologie et en science des matériaux."

#: src/lib/units.ts:618
msgid "A square yard equals about 0.836 square metres. Carpeting, fabric, and landscaping frequently quote area in square yards."
msgstr "Un mètre carré équivaut à environ 0,836 mètre carré. La moquette, les tissus et l'aménagement paysager indiquent souvent une superficie en mètres carrés."

#: src/lib/units-mass-motion.ts:128
msgid "A stone equals 14 avoirdupois pounds, or exactly 6.35029318 kilograms. Body weight in the United Kingdom is still often quoted in stones and pounds."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:278
msgid "A surveyor's chain (Gunter's chain) equals 66 feet, or about 20.117 metres. It was foundational to land surveying in English-speaking countries."
msgstr "Une chaîne d'arpenteur (chaîne de Gunter) équivaut à 66 pieds, soit environ 20,117 mètres. C’était un fondement de l’arpentage dans les pays anglophones."

#: src/lib/units.ts:501
msgid "A temperature scale used primarily in the United States."
msgstr "Échelle de température utilisée principalement aux États-Unis."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2301
msgid "A time zone changes how we label the same instant (“15:00 UTC” vs “11:00 EDT”). A duration unit measures how much time elapses between two instants (3 hours, 180 minutes). Converting 3 hours to minutes never requires a time zone. Scheduling a call across zones never changes how long 3 hours lasts."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1646
msgid "A typical pattern is: dimensional weight = (L × W × H) / divisor, with L, W, H in centimetres or inches and the result in kilograms or pounds matching the divisor’s definition. Divisors differ by air vs ground and by carrier. Always use the divisor printed for your service level."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1209
msgid "A unit choice cannot fix a poor measurement. It can only present the measurement clearly. State uncertainties and significant figures honestly after conversion. Converting an uncertain value into a flashy tiny unit does not make the measurement more precise."
msgstr "Un choix d’unité ne peut pas corriger une mauvaise mesure. Il ne peut que présenter clairement la mesure. Indiquez honnêtement les incertitudes et les chiffres significatifs après la conversion. Convertir une valeur incertaine en une petite unité flashy ne rend pas la mesure plus précise."

